<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan seeks financial adviser for bank sale.</title>
<headline>Pakistan seeks financial adviser for bank sale.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Privatisation Commission is seeking a financial adviser for the sale of all or part of the government's 49 percent stake in Allied Bank Limited, the official news agency APP reported on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the commission had invited interested parties to express interest by 1000 GMT on May 15.</p>
<p>The adviser will conduct due diligence and valuation, structure the transaction, assist in the placement and flotation of shares, and arrange underwriting and incidental services.</p>
<p>-- Islamabad 9251-274757</p>
</text>
